  "response": "## Bayesian calculation\n\n**Given:**\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002\n- Sensitivity: P(T+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(T–|D̄) = 0.95 → false positive rate P(T+|D̄) = 0.05\n\n**Bayes' theorem:**\n\n$$P(D|T+) = \\frac{P(T+|D)P(D)}{P(T+|D)P(D) + P(T+|\\bar D)P(\\bar D)}$$\n\n$$= \\frac{0.98 \\times 0.002}{0.98 \\times 0.002 + 0.05 \\times 0.998}$$\n\n$$= \\frac{0.00196}{0.00196 + 0.0499} = \\frac{0.00196}{0.05186} = \\frac{98}{2593} \\approx 0.0377941$$\n\n**Result:** ≈ 3.7794% → **3.78%**\n\nIntuition check: among 500,000 people, ~1,000 have the condition and ~980 test positive (98% sensitivity). Among the 499,000 without it, 5% false-positive → ~24,950 false positives. So P(D|T+) = 980/(980+24,950) = 980/25,930 ≈ 3.78%. ✓ Matches.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
